# Optional benchmark manifest (aura_worker.eval.manifest): local real
# recordings + reference MIDI for `python -m aura_worker.eval.benchmark
# --manifest ...`. Conventional local location; the --manifest flag itself
# accepts any path, this just keeps the default one out of git.
docs/benchmarks/manifest*.json
docs/benchmarks/manifest_data/

# DQ-2 (piano transcription model): the pretrained checkpoint (~164MB, CC-BY-4.0,
# see docs/benchmarks/2026-08-21-dq2.md) is fetched at BUILD time by
# workers/transcription/scripts/fetch_piano_weights.py, checksum-verified, never
# committed to git (no git-lfs in this repo -- see that script's module docstring
# for why a build-time fetch was chosen over vendoring).
workers/transcription/weights/

# apps/desktop/aura-backend.spec is a PyInstaller-GENERATED file
# (build-backend.sh's `pyinstaller ... --specpath apps/desktop` rewrites it
# fresh on every run) -- it was previously tracked by mistake and baked in
# a contributor's local absolute path (--add-data's source path is
# resolved to an absolute path at generation time), which is misleading to
# read and has no reason to be version-controlled since the real build
# never reads the committed copy, only ever regenerates its own.
apps/desktop/aura-backend.spec
